cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Osteosarcoma ALT: a transcriptomic classification signature and a
  pre-registered test of TCAB1-stratified BIR dependency
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rizvanov
    given-names: Rinat
    email: 1812Rinat@gmail.com
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/rinatrizvanov/osteosarcoma-alt-dependency-research
abstract: >-
  Two linked computational projects on alternative lengthening of telomeres
  (ALT) in osteosarcoma, using DepMap 26Q1. Part 1 builds a 19-gene curated
  transcriptomic ALT classifier (primary cohort N = 20, AUROC 0.948,
  permutation p < 0.001) and reports a bootstrap coefficient-stability analysis
  showing that only FANCM and TERT are stable across cohorts. Part 2 uses the
  frozen ALT labels to pre-register and test the prediction that ALT+ lines
  with low TCAB1/WRAP53 expression depend more on break-induced replication
  (POLD3, RAD52, SMARCAL1) than on canonical homologous recombination (BRCA1,
  BRCA2, RAD51). The test did not confirm the prediction (Cliff's delta =
  +0.281, p = 0.382, opposite to the predicted direction), and a subsequent
  four-iteration pre-registered campaign under experiment-wide Benjamini-
  Hochberg correction produced no positive result (final q = 0.420, 0.420,
  1.000). The repository documents why the endpoint could not have detected
  the effect: two of its three BIR genes carry no dependency variation in this
  cohort, and 68.2 percent of the composite's variance came from the
  comparator arm. No claim is made that the biological hypothesis is false.
keywords:
  - alternative lengthening of telomeres
  - osteosarcoma
  - DepMap
  - CRISPR gene dependency
  - break-induced replication
  - TCAB1
  - WRAP53
  - SMARCAL1
  - pre-registration
  - null result
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-13'
